# Studio env contract. Only vars prefixed SANITY_STUDIO_ are exposed to the
# Studio bundle. Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and adjust per environment.
# All values here are PUBLIC by nature (they ship in the Studio bundle).

# Front-end origin the Presentation tool loads in its iframe for Preview /
# Visual Editing. Defaults to the local Next.js app when unset in DEVELOPMENT.
# REQUIRED for a production build (`sanity build`/`sanity deploy`): the build
# throws if it is unset (previewUrl.ts), because a deployed Studio that falls
# back to localhost can't reach the front end and Visual Editing never connects
# (#193). Point it at the deployed app per Studio deployment (the Vercel prod
# origin); never hardcode a production URL in sanity.config.ts.
# The production value is committed in `studio/.env.production` (loaded only in
# production mode, so `sanity deploy` works with no inline var while `sanity dev`
# keeps this localhost default). For DEV, override here or in a gitignored
# `.env.local` if your Next app runs on a different port.
# Must be a valid ABSOLUTE origin (e.g. https://example.com) with NO trailing
# slash — the value passes straight through to previewUrl.initial, so a
# malformed value breaks the preview iframe at runtime.
SANITY_STUDIO_PREVIEW_URL=http://localhost:3000
